Description: Fix C++23 incomplete type error with std::unique_ptr<MediaLog> default parameter
 C++23 with libc++ introduced strict static_assert(sizeof(_Tp) >= 0) in
 std::unique_ptr destructor. When a function default parameter uses
 std::unique_ptr<T> with an incomplete type T (forward-declared), the
 compiler instantiates the destructor at the declaration point, triggering
 the sizeof check.
 .
 Note: The simpler = {} value initialization fix does NOT work for this case
 because the destructor is still instantiated at the declaration point for
 static function default parameters.
 .
 This fix uses function overloading instead of default parameters:
 - Add a 5-parameter overload (without media_log, helper_cb, task_runner)
 - Keep the 8-parameter version but remove default values
 - The short overload forwards to the full version with nullptr/default values
 .
 This pattern avoids destructor instantiation in the header while maintaining
 API compatibility for all callers.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-27

